1
00:03:51,818 --> 00:03:57,818
You don't need extraordinary powers to do extraordinary things.

2
00:07:43,636 --> 00:07:49,636
The Wild Thornberrys Movie is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Cathy Malkasian.

3
00:11:35,454 --> 00:11:41,454
Eliza and Debbie are two sisters who don't always get along.

4
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
But their relationship is put to the test when Debbie's life is in danger, and
Eliza might have to give up her power to talk to animals....

5
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:25,090
Eliza Thornberry (voice), played by Lacey Chabert.

6
00:23:10,909 --> 00:23:16,909
Darwin (voice), played by Tom Kane.

7
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
Phaedra (voice), played by Cree Summer.

8
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Nigel Thornberry (voice), played by Tim Curry.

9
00:34:46,363 --> 00:34:52,363
Cordelia Thornberry (voice), played by Lynn Redgrave.

10
00:38:38,181 --> 00:38:44,181
Debbie Thornberry (voice), played by Danielle Harris.

11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
The Wild Thornberrys Movie is a 2002 American animated adventure comedy film
produced by Klasky Csupo, based on the television series.

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
It was written by Kate Boutilier, and features the voices of Lacey Chabert, Tom Kane, Danielle
Harris, Jodi Carlisle, Tim Curry, Lynn Redgrave, Rupert Everett, Marisa Tomei, and Flea.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
The film follows Eliza Thornberry as she goes on a quest to
save a cheetah cub from ruthless poachers.

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
It is the first installment in The Wild Thornberrys film series.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
The film's music score was written by series composer Drew Neumann.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
The Wild Thornberrys Movie was released on December 20, 2002, by
Paramount Pictures through their Nickelodeon Movies label.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
It received positive reviews and grossed $61 million worldwide.

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
The film was nominated for Best Original Song at the 75th Academy
Awards for Paul Simon's "Father and Daughter".

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
A sequel, and a crossover with characters from Rugrats
titled Rugrats Go Wild, was released in 2003.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of sibling relationship,
safari, villain, wildlife, baboon.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
